abstract: >-
  An empirical, regulation-anchored benchmark comparing static and runtime
  detection of seeded cloud misconfigurations in Terraform-based Azure
  fintech payment workloads. Seven detection tools (four static analysers and
  three runtime mechanisms) are evaluated across fifteen deployment variants
  and ten seeded misconfigurations, reporting true-positive rate, false-positive
  rate, and time-to-first-detection with 95% confidence intervals, McNemar
  paired tests, and set-cover complementarity analysis. The repository contains
  all Terraform variants, seeded-misconfiguration flags, the custom KQL rule
  set, the analysis harness, and raw normalised tool outputs.
